From 0ae66c3a95763bf585bac54467d56cca227e234f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:18:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hds cache: a write updates every set that holds the sector

Sets start at the LBA that missed, so two can overlap (e.g. the boot-time 0x20/0x21 -> 2/3
remap). Updating only the first match let a later read return the old sector from the other set
once the first was evicted. Harmless in practice here (8-sector sets that are almost always
page-aligned), but it corrupted data in the PZL rewrite's 32-sector cache. Found by Charlie.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
---
 src/hdscache.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hdscache.c b/src/hdscache.c
index 0cc498c..7ff6df8 100644
--- a/src/hdscache.c
+++ b/src/hdscache.c
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ int hds_cache_write(struct smb2_context *smb2, struct smb2fh *sfh, uint32_t lba,
         struct cache *c = &cache[i];
         if (c->sfh == sfh && c->smb2 == smb2 && lba >= c->lba && lba < c->lba + c->sects) {
             memcpy(&c->data[(lba - c->lba) * SECTOR_SIZE], buf, SECTOR_SIZE);
-            break;
+            /* break しない: 組は読み損ねた LBA から始まるので重なることがある (起動の LBA 0x20/0x21 -> 2/3 の
+               差し替えなど)。1 つ目だけ直すと、それが追い出されたあと別の組から古い中身を返す (PZL で見つかった) */
         }
     }
 
